  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "r0b0tlab’s single-GB10 native-SM121 vLLM profile for Poolside Laguna S 2.1 NVFP4, on the checkpoint pair the kit declares in its production runtime manifest, primary 07614121 and its quantization-matched DFlash-NVFP4 drafter 72379475 (the later August 2026 pair, 826aacdf and b3b5921a, which ships a native 1,048,576-token context, is not used). This recipe keeps the upstream adapter’s source-qualified 262,144-token / 32-sequence profile, FlashInfer attention, FlashInfer-CUTLASS NVFP4 experts, FP8 KV, and DFlash K=7. The specialized image remains pinned to r0b0tlab’s immutable vLLM 0.25.1 SM121/FlashInfer build; Poolside requires vLLM 0.25.0 or later and the model is loaded from mounted files with trust-remote-code. The source repository’s measured performance and quality evidence is bound to this pair (its scripts/verify_release.py names another primary revision, 216d1f13, an inconsistency inside the kit); target and draft compatibility, context behavior, memory fit, tool behavior, and output quality remain unverified here. Licences: target OpenMDW 1.1; package MIT; vLLM Apache-2.0; draft card declares no licence (information only).",
